 - area                                                                                               
   target table: AreaInformation  (NOT POI — separate table)                                          
   blockInfo:                                                                                         
     action: 'BRIC:area'                                                                              
     category: "Navigation"                                                                           
     description: "Select area / floor / session"                                                     
     enabled: true                                                                                    
     parameters[]: 3 cascading dropdowns                                                              
       - area: rows from AreaInformation.area column (full string, e.g. "LG sciencepark W10")         
         type: 'string'                                                                               
         options[]:                                                                                   
           value: area        ← full string from DB column                                            
           display_name: area ← same                                                                  
       - floor: JSON keys from AreaInformation.information column (e.g. "1", "2", "M", "B1")          
         type: 'string'                                                                               
         options[]:                                                                                   
           value: floor                                                                               
           display_name: floor                                                                        
           area: area  ← used by cascading JS                                                         
       - session: JSON array values for each floor in AreaInformation.information                     
           e.g. information = {"1": ["default", "elevator_AB"], ...}                                  
         type: 'string'                                                                               
         options[]:                                                                                   
           value: session_string                                                                      
           display_name: session_string                                                               
           area: area   ← used by cascading JS                                                        
           floor: floor ← used by cascading JS                                                        
                                                                                                      
   AreaInformation table columns:                                                                     
     id, area, information (JSON: {floor: [session_string, ...], ...})                                
                                                                                                      
   Cascading behavior (generator_engine.py / emit_block_file):                                        
     - Detect action == 'BRIC:area' in the blocks list                                                
     - Build POI_TREE: { area: { floor: [[session, session], ...] } }                                 
       from session parameter's raw_options (area+floor metadata)                                     
     - Inside the registrar function, inject cascading validator closure:                             
         areaField → rebuilds floor options + session options                                         
         floorField → rebuilds session options for current area                                       
         setDropdownOpts: uses field.setOptions() if available, falls back to menuGenerator_          
     - BT export: standard Action node { action: "BRIC:area", parameter: { area, floor, session } }   
                                                                                                      
   Implementation (db_sync.py):                                                                       
     _fetch_area_information_rows(client): SELECT area, information FROM AreaInformation              
       → parses information JSON → returns [{area, information: {floor: [sessions]}}]                 
     _BRIC_AREA_TEMPLATE: seeded with placeholder options to force dropdown generation                
     _ensure_bric_area_block(path): inserts before other BRIC blocks if absent                        
     _update_area_block_options(path, area_info_rows): builds area/floor/session options              
       area opts: [{value: area, display_name: area}] — FULL string from DB column                    
       floor opts: unique (area, floor) pairs with area metadata                                      
       session opts: unique (area, floor, session) triples with area+floor metadata                   



- move_to_pos: This block use the parameter in DB.                                                   
  target table: POI                                                                                  
  blockInfo:                                                                                         
    action: 'BRIC.POI:navigation/move_to_pose'                                                       
    category: "Navigation"                                                                           
    name: "navigation/move_to_pose"                                                                  
    description: "Point of Interest — move to named pose"                                            
    enabled: true                                                                                    
    robot_type                                                                                       
    parameters[]: refer to the target table.                                                         
      name: 'name'                                                                                   
      type: 'string'                                                                                 
      description: 'Point of Interest'                                                               
      options[]: Column mapping from DB table POI.                                                   
        - value: name                                                                                
          display_name: display_name (area-prefixed when same name appears in multiple areas,        
            e.g. "LG sciencepark W10 › Hanging Rack")                                                
          description: description                                                                   
          area: area  ← stored for future area-based filtering                                       
          robot_type: robot_type (default: "", for robot type filtering)                             
          operation_profile: operation_profile (default:"", for profile filtering)                   
      Notes:                                                                                         
        - Duplicate names across areas are distinguished via area-prefixed display_name              
          (_poi_display_name helper in db_sync.py)                                                   
        - All POI rows (across all areas) are shown; no runtime cross-block filtering yet            
  reference_file: POI.json                                                                           
    Each entry uses raw DB `name` as key:                                                            
      { "name": "{name}", "data": { "pose_type": "map", "pose": { "x": ..., "y": ..., "z": ... } } } 
    Manual entries (e.g. PickUp, Dump, PutDown) are preserved if not in DB.                          
    DB entries with duplicate (area,floor,name) composites are deduplicated.                         
